  "knob_detail": {
    "description": "After hold_days >= 2 (48h on the daily calendar), flatten the open long if cumulative funding paid is a net cost AND gross unrealized P&L is below +1R. Existing exits (MA50, RSI, 30d time stop, BE stop, RISK-OFF, DD defense) keep same-bar priority. BE arming unchanged (still avg_entry on confirm; jugular trail avg_entry*1.02).",
    "hold_threshold_hours": 48,
    "hold_threshold_days": 2,
    "one_r_definition": "Engine has no explicit initial risk stop at probe/confirm. 1R proxy = 3% of avg_entry applied to current notional (dollar 1R = 0.03 * total_notional). Matches the +3% probe-gain gate that arms confirmation and premature BE. Unrealized R uses GROSS price P&L vs that 1R; funding is the cost being cut, not part of the R tape.",
    "one_r_pct": 0.03,
    "adverse_funding_definition": "Cumulative funding paid on the open position is a net cost (funding_so_far > 0). Official engine longs always pay the average 8h funding rate, so this is true for every long with hold_days > 0.",
    "unrealized_measure": "gross_price_pnl = (close-avg_entry)/avg_entry * notional; flatten if gross_price_pnl < 1R",
